{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Behold, his bedstead — a bedstead of iron.</b> The sense of ערש is a fortified city, a tower, and a fortress, like בפאת מטה ובדמשק ערש. And in the language of the Talmud they call every district ערסייתא, meaning a fortress surrounded by a strong wall, like iron." "<b>Nine cubits its length.</b> The height of the wall around the fortress, and four cubits its width — the width of the wall." "<b>By the cubit of a man.</b> By the cubit of any person who is not a small child."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The two biblical citations in the second sentence are left untranslated as they appear in the source without being expounded."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:28.637826685Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}